@@ -139,6 +139,12 @@ states. The fork action defaults to the latest completed `turn/end` boundary,
 creates the corresponding Nexent child conversation, and navigates directly to
 its inherited trajectory view.
 
+Each recorded model request also carries the active smolagents tool definitions
+in the Event v0 `request/header.header.tools` field. The integration reuses the
+same schema conversion as the model request instead of maintaining a second
+Nexent-specific schema shape. This lets the retained DSH detail panel resolve a
+Tool call by `callId` and render its Parameters, Result, Schema, and Timing tabs.
+
 The frontend packages are committed as reproducible tarballs under
 `frontend/vendor/` and were packed from Perix runtime data commit
 `3a1f931ddcd7f94944789a195536208405b7182d`:
@@ -167,7 +173,12 @@ Run each file in its own pytest process, matching Nexent's repository test
 runner. The acceptance test launches fresh Python processes from outside the
 repository root, verifies that `perix_event` resolves from `site-packages`,
 executes a real `CoreAgent` tool call, resumes the parent Session, forks it, and
-independently continues the child.
+independently continues the child. Its long-trajectory case writes 10 Turns in
+one process, cold-resumes the same Session for another 10 Turns in a new
+process, forks at the completed boundary, and then appends distinct Turn 21
+suffixes to the parent and child. The inherited 189-Event prefix must remain
+exactly equal and the recorded Tool schema must match smolagents' request
+schema.
 
 Run the frontend trajectory and regression checks from `frontend/`:
 
